      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.046,
            0.364,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.087,
            0.808,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": "See if you can describe all possible lengths of the third side in each case, so that a triangle exists with those sidelengths. For example, in case (a), all numbers strictly between 99 and 101 would be possible."
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.823,
            0.077,
            0.924,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": "Try This"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.186,
            0.847,
            0.236
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "7.3 Construction of Triangles When Some Sides and Angles are Given"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.245,
            0.848,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": "We have seen how to construct triangles when their sidelengths are given. Now, we will take up constructions where in place of some sidelengths, angle measures are given."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.319,
            0.569,
            0.341
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Two Sides and the Included Angle"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.35,
            0.848,
            0.409
          ],
          "content": "How do we construct a triangle if two sides and the angle included between them are given? Here are some examples of measurements showing the included angle."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.412,
            0.325,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.229,
                0.537,
                0.27,
                0.551
              ],
              "content": "4 cm"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.373,
            0.414,
            0.622,
            0.533
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.699,
            0.407,
            0.824,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.571,
            0.789,
            0.594
          ],
          "content": "Construct a triangle ABC with AB = 5 cm, AC = 4 cm and $\\angle A = 45^{\\circ}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.602,
            0.814,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": "Let us take one of the given sides, AB, as the base of the triangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.351,
            0.626,
            0.644,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.798,
            0.574,
            0.817
          ],
          "content": "**Step 1:** Construct a side AB of length 5 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.816,
            0.578,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": "**Step 2:** Construct $\\angle \\mathrm{A} = 45^{\\circ}$ by drawing the other arm of the angle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.853,
            0.579,
            0.89
          ],
          "content": "**Step 3:** Mark the point C on the other arm such that AC = 4 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.89,
            0.577,
            0.911
          ],
          "content": "**Step 4:** Join BC to get the required triangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.591,
            0.771,
            0.866,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": "",
